A [[human]] [[Gender|male]] '''Jedi youngling''' came to be trained by the [[Jedi Order]] sometime before the [[Mission to Mustafar|end]] of the [[Clone Wars]]. In [[19 BBY]], he was present at the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on [[Coruscant]] when the newly appointed [[Sith Lord]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] led an [[Operation: Knightfall|attack]] against the [[Jedi]]. The young boy was slain by Vader within the [[Jedi Council Chamber]], becoming one of the first victims of the [[Great Jedi Purge]].

==Biography==
===A short life===
{{Quote|First I want you to go to the Jedi Temple. We will catch them off-balance. Do what must be done, Lord Vader. Do not hesitate. Show no mercy.|Darth Sidious, instructing his new apprentice to assault the Jedi Grand Temple|<ref name="ROTS" />}}
The [[youngling]] was initiated into the [[Jedi Order]] at some point during the final [[Standard year|years]] of the [[Republic Era]] and trained in the [[Jedi]] arts<ref name="DB Younglings" /> during the [[Clone Wars]], a [[The galaxy|pan-galactic]] conflict between the [[Galactic Republic]] and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]]. [[Gender|He]] was taught within the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on [[Coruscant]] shortly before the [[Mission to Mustafar|end]] of the war.<ref name="ROTS" /> In [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Date note" /> the [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] was turned to the [[Dark side of the Force|dark side]] by [[Darth Sidious]], who convinced the young man that all Jedi had become [[Treason|enemies]] of the Republic. He ordered Skywalker, now under the moniker of [[Darth]] Vader, to [[Death|kill]] all members of the Order within the Jedi [[Jedi temple|Temple's]] walls.<ref name="ROTS" />

[[File:Bandeam.png|thumb|left|200px|The youngling directly before being killed by Darth Vader.]]
Vader led the [[501st Legion]] of the [[Grand Army of the Republic]] in a [[Operation: Knightfall|siege]] on the Temple, marching into the building and decimating the Jedi within. The youngling and several other [[Jedi Initiate|initiates]] fled to the [[Jedi Council Chamber]], hiding behind the chairs the [[Jedi High Council|Council members]] would sit in. Vader later entered the chamber, prompting the youngling, who recognized the Jedi hero, to reveal himself and ask Skywalker what they would do against the [[clone trooper]]s that outnumbered them. To the child's shock, however, the [[Sith Lord]] ignited his [[Skywalker lightsaber|lightsaber]] and proceeded to slaughter the younglings.<ref name="ROTS" />

===Legacy===
{{Quote|All of the Jedi? Even the Younglings?''"<br />"''All of them''|Darth Sidious and Vader discuss the extermination of the Jedi, including Younglings.|<ref name="DV 7">[[Darth Vader (2020) 7|''Darth Vader'' (2020) 7]]</ref>}}
Afterwards, Vader, visibly distraught, informed Sidious that all of the Jedi, including the Jedi Younglings, had been killed. Sidious, pleased, then ordered Vader to "go and bring peace" to his new [[Galactic Empire|Empire]].<ref name="DV 7" />

Vader's murder of the youngling and his comrades would be uncovered by [[Jedi Master]]s [[Yoda]] and [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]]. After Sidious declared himself [[Galactic Emperor|leader]] of a newly christened Galactic Empire, Kenobi informed Skywalker's [[Marriage|wife]], [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]], of the crimes her husband had committed. Initially refusing to believe that he was capable of killing children, Amidala later confronted Vader on [[Mustafar]], where she discovered that the man she loved had indeed fallen to the dark side.<ref name="ROTS" />

The youngling's death would go on to be one of many counted among the [[Great Jedi Purge]], Sidious' quest to eradicate the [[galaxy]] of the Jedi Order, though some Jedi managed to survive.<ref name="ROTS" /> By [[18 BBY]],<ref name="Ferren Barr Date">According to ''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]'', the occupation of Mon Cala took place a year into the [[Darth Sidious|Emperor's]] rule. Since ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the beginning of Imperial rule to [[19 BBY]], the occupation of Mon Cala took place in [[18 BBY]].</ref> the renegade Padawan [[Ferren Barr]] had learned of Skywalker's betrayal, including his murder of the younglings, and kept files about the Purge within his [[R1-series astromech droid]] [[Endee]]. He later informed [[Ferren Barr's disciples|his disciples]] of the children's death at Vader's [[Limb|hand]] during the [[Invasion of Mon Cala]].<ref name="DLotS 14">[[Darth Vader (2017) 14|''Darth Vader'' (2017) 14]]</ref>

In [[3 ABY]],<ref name=Timelines>''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> while he was injured on Mustafar and hunted by [[Sith assassin]] [[Ochi of Bestoon]] on Sidious's orders, Vader had a vision of him killing the Younglings and informing Sidious about their deaths. After the vision, he declared that neither Sidious, nor he, nor anyone else would know peace ever again.<ref name="DV 7" />

Later in 3 ABY,<ref name="Date">{{OutlawsComicDate|Darth Vader (2020) 24|''Darth Vader'' (2020) 24}}</ref> on [[Gabredor III]], Vader and the former [[Naboo Royal Handmaidens|Naboo Handmaiden]] [[Sabé]] mounted an [[Attack on the science colony|attack]] on the [[science colony]] of the corrupt [[Governor]] [[Tauntaza]]. During the attack, the pair freed several conscripts, who expressed guilt over working for Tauntaza. While Sabé reassured the conscripts they were innocent of Tauntaza's crimes, Vader experienced several flashbacks to his own violent actions, including the slaughter of the Youngling.<ref name="DV 24> [[Darth Vader (2020) 24|''Darth Vader'' (2020) 24]]</ref>

==Personality and traits==
The youngling was a [[human]] male child with [[Color|blond]] [[hair]] and blue [[eye]]s. He had fair skin and, shortly before his death, red cheeks. He was trusting of Jedi Knight Anakin Skywalker, looking to the older individual to guide the younglings against the [[Cloning|clone]] [[trooper]] threat.<ref name="ROTS" />

==Equipment==
Like other Jedi initiates, the youngling dressed in standard [[Jedi apparel]],<ref name="Secrets of the Jedi">''[[Star Wars: The Secrets of the Jedi]]''</ref> including a sandy-colored tunic and a brown belt and boots. He also had a [[Padawan braid]] draped from his head. When he was threatened by [[Lord]] Vader on Coruscant, he held a [[lightsaber]].<ref name="ROTS" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|The youngling scene &ndash; you know the one &ndash; was added during pick-ups.|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|<ref name="Pablo pick up">{{Twitter|pabl0hidalgo|status/1428600400219820032|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|quote=The youngling scene &ndash; you know the one &ndash; was added during pick-ups.|archivedate=20220301002032}}</ref>}}
The youngling first appeared in the [[2005]] film [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']], the final installment of the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[prequel trilogy]],<ref name="ROTS" /> in a scene shot during pick-ups.<ref name="Pablo pick up" /> Although unnamed in ''Star Wars'' [[canon]], he was identified as [[Sors Bandeam]] in the [[Star Wars Legends|Legends continuity]]. He was portrayed in an uncredited performance by [[Ross Beadman]], whose name served as the basis for the character's in-universe title.<ref name="Ross' Story">{{YouTube|video=xfCdh8OgA7w|text=Star Wars Exclusive Interview: Sors Bandeam|channel=channel/UCrSaCvf4KskVl2GzLw2UQhA|name=Spicy Coconut Productions|archivedate=20200815101913}}</ref> The youngling scene has taken on a degree of infamy since release.<ref name="Pablo pick up" />

